WEBVTT

00:00:00.004 --> 00:00:03.845
How to use: WildTrace in 2 minutes. Ask a question. Get the answer, its sources and its limits.

00:00:03.945 --> 00:00:08.349
Ask: The Atlas opens with a question, not a dashboard.

00:00:08.449 --> 00:00:10.970
Ask: Say who you are, and the questions change to fit.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:16.941
Question 1 of 3: Is wildlife sold online ever caught?

00:00:17.041 --> 00:00:20.877
Question 1: Every answer: one line, its number and a chart.

00:00:20.977 --> 00:00:24.406
Question 1: Who answers: each source is named and linked.

00:00:24.506 --> 00:00:28.899
Question 1: And what the number cannot tell you.

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:36.725
Question 2 of 3: Where does seized red sanders go?

00:00:36.825 --> 00:00:41.705
Question 2: Flows: seized shipments reported to CITES, from source to market.

00:00:41.805 --> 00:00:47.772
Question 2: Lines shade green at the source, blue in transit, amber at the market.

00:00:47.872 --> 00:00:52.713
Question 2: Evidence: what was seized, when, who reported it, and the news.

00:00:52.813 --> 00:01:02.214
Question 3 of 3: How accurate is WildTrace?

00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:11.688
Question 3: Measured, not asserted: a blind audit of 200 random cases.

00:01:11.788 --> 00:01:14.519
Question 3: Each case: a plain account and its evidence grade.

00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:22.617
Question 3: Every source is listed with its outlet. Nobody accused is ever named.

00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:30.177
Tools: Investigate: a link chart, plus your own data, kept in your browser.

00:01:30.277 --> 00:01:34.098
Tools: Analysis: the whole record on one sheet.

00:01:34.198 --> 00:01:38.842
WildTrace · Follow the trade: Open data, free to reuse. Every answer has a citable page · download every case as CSV · DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22902819
